    "ls|LS17_S14_U_117": "�\n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EDUCATION \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION \n \nLOK SABHA  \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *117 \nANSWERED ON 11.12.2023 \n \nOnline Coaching Platform-SATHEE \n \n*117.  SHRI BHOLA SINGH: \nSHRI VINOD KUMAR SONKAR: \n \nWill the Minister of EDUCATION be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Ministry in collaboration with IIT -Kanpur has launched online coaching platform \nSelf-Assessment Test and Help for Entrance Exams (SATHEE); \n(b) if so, the details thereof; \n(c) whether the SATHEE is an open learning platform available to students at no cost; \n(d) if so, whether SATHEE has launched a 45 -days crash course for aspirants and it hosts live \nand recorded lectures, expertly designed curriculum and doubt-clearing sessions for students; \n(e) whether the portal uses Artificial Intelligence (AI) to interact with students and can be \n�������������������������������������������������������������������������������������������� \n(f) if so, the details thereof; and \n(g) the steps taken by the Government to provide quality education in remote areas as well? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF EDUCATION \n(SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n \n \n(a) to (g): A Statement is laid on the table of the House. \n \n***** \n  \n\n�\n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO ( g) IN RESPECT OF  LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *1 17 FOR REPLY  ON 11.12.2023 �������������������� ��ONLINE \nCOACHING PLATFORM -SATHEE��ASKED BY SHRI BHOLA SINGH , SHRI VINOD KUMAR \nSONKAR�������������������������������������������������������������������� \n \n(a) to (f) Department of Higher Education in collaboration with IIT Kanpur has started SATHEE  \n(Self-Assessment, Test and Help for Entrance Examination) portal to provide quality education \nto every student who inten d to participate in competitive examination such as JEE, NEET and \nvarious State level Engineering and other Examination. \n \nThis portal has several facilities to help students for such examination that includes: - \n  \n- Solve with Me : a senior student who has passed a competitive exam, solves mock test \npapers and explains his or her thought process to solve different questions on camera. The \nsession is telecasted live as well as recording is shared with the aspirants. This helps aspiring \nstudents to understand the tips to ace a question paper beyond just subject knowledge. \n \n- ",
    "ls|LS17_S14_U_118": "������������������� �\n��������������������� �\n������������������������������ �\n������\n�\n��������� �\n������������������������ �\n���������������������� �\n�\n�������������������������� �\n����������������������������������������������������\nWill the Minister of Education be pleased to state the details of the research works \nundertaken on the culture of tribal areas and folk literature of Himachal Pradesh by \nthe students of Central University situated in Dharamshala? \n \n \n������ �\n�\n��������������������� �\n������������������������� �\n�\nA statement is laid on the Table of the House.  \n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n�\n\n������������������ ������������ ������ �������������������������\n�������������������������������� ������������������ �����������������\n������������������������ ������������� �����������������������\n��������������� �\nCentre for Tribal Studies provides Post Graduate Diploma and Ph.D. Programme in Central \nUniversity of Himachal Pradesh. The area for PG Diploma programme broadly includes �� \ncustom, tradition, culture of Indian tribal communities, tribal policies and legislations, \nendangered tribal communities and their languages, historical perspective of tribal policies, tribal \ncommunities of Himachal Pradesh etc.   \nResearch work undertaken by the in PhD Scholars in the University:  \n• Study of social and cultural heritage of Ghirth caste (a study in the context of Kangra \ndistrict) \n• Folklore of Tangsa Tribe in Arunachal Pradesh: A socio-cultural study \n• The Concept of Tribe in Colonial India: A Study \n• Hygiene Management among Adolescent Girls of Gaddi Tribe in Bharmour (H.P) \n• Social and cultural study of Gaddi tribe (with special reference to Himachal Pradesh) \n• Studying the reach and impact of New Media on the Tribal communities in Himachal \nPradesh \n• An exploratory study of the Lavanya community of Kashmir. \n• Gujjar Community: Gotra System and Communication Traditions \nApart from the above research work, Janjatiya Gaurav Diwas was also organized at the Centre \nfor Tribal Studies of Himachal Pradesh Central University. Students were made aware about the \ntribal culture of Himachal Pradesh and the economic, social and geographical conditions of the \ntribal areas of Himachal Pradesh through several activities held on the occasion of Janjatiya \nGaurav Diwas.  \n*** ",
    "ls|LS17_S14_U_119": " \n \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EDUCATION \nDEPARTMENT OF SCHOOL EDUCATION & LITERACY \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO:- 119 \nANSWERED ON-11/12/2023 \n \n                                                     Vacancy of B.Ed Seats \n        \n \n*119.  SHRI SYED IMTIAZ JALEEL:   \nWill the Minister of EDUCATION be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government is aware that 6008 B.Ed seats remain vacant out of total 34830 seats in the \nState of Maharashtra and if so, the details thereof; \n(b) the details of the steps taken by the Government to address the root cause behind the substantial \nnumber of vacant B.Ed seats; \n(c) whether the Government plans to improve the admission process to ensure maximum utilisation of \navailable seats and if so, the details thereof; and \n(d) whether the Government is aware of the concern regarding the lack of interest among the youth in \npursuing B.Ed, if so, the measures being considered by Government to enhance the recruitment of \nteachers in educational institutions? \nA N S W E R \n \nMINISTER OF EDUCATION \n(SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n \n(a) to (d):  A statement is laid on the table of the House. \n \n*** \n \n \n  \n\n \n \n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d ) OF LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 119 FOR REPLY ON 11th DECEMBER, 2023 ASKED BY HON’BLE MEMBER \nOF PARLIAMENT SHRI SYED IMTIAZ JALEEL REGRADING VACANCY OF B.ED. SEATS \n \n \n(a) : The Government of Maharashtra has informed that in the academic year  2023-24, out of a total \n34,830 B.Ed. seats from 477 B.Ed. colleges in Maharashtra, 4,785 seats remain vacant.  \n \n(b) & (c) : The Government of Maharashtra has also informed that in order to ensure maximum \nutilisation of available seats, interaction programme s were  carried out throughout Maharashtra before \ncommencement of centralised admission process for B.Ed . 2023 to create awareness among candidates, \nparents, institutes and other stakeholders. Further, extension of registration period for B.Ed . course for \nforty-four days, extension of the last round of counselling for four days were also given by the \nGovernment of Maharashtra to provide opportunity to unadmitted candidates.  \n \nThe Government of India is concerned about integrity, credibility, efficacy and quality of teacher \neducation in the country. As per recommendations of NEP 2020, the Government has notified Integrated \nTeacher Education Programme (ITEP) & its pi lot is being conducted from 2023 -24 in Higher Education \nInstitutions (HEIs) with accreditation of NAAC A and above. Admission to the ITEP Pilot is through \nadmission tests conducted by the National Testing Agency (NTA). \n \n(d) : For enhancing recruitment of teachers , the Ministry of Education, from time to time, through \nreview meetings and advisories, requests the State Governments and UT Administrations for filling up \nvacant posts of teachers and their rational deployment. Further, the Central Government through the \nCentrally Sponsored Scheme of Samagra Shiksh a provides financial assistance to the States and UTs to \nmaintain appropriate Pupil-Teacher Ratio (PTR) for various levels of schooling, as per norms prescribed \nin the Right of Children to Free and Compulsory Education (RTE) Act, 2009, as amended from time to \ntime. \n*** \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S14_U_12": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EDUCATION \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION \n \nLOK SABHA  \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *12 \nANSWERED ON 04.12.2023 \n \nOne Nation One Student ID \n \n*12.  PROF. RITA BAHUGUNA JOSHI: \nDR. SHRIKANT EKNATH SHINDE: \n \nWill the Minister of EDUCATION be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the details of ‘One Nation, One Student ID’ initiative under Automated Permanent \nAcademic Account Registry (APAAR) and its key objectives; \n(b) whether there is any role and involvement of the Ministry in this initiative; \n(c) whether it aligns with the National Education Policy (NEP) 2020’s emphasis on gender \nparity and equal opportunities in education; \n(d) the details of the enrolment process for APAAR followed by schools and the role of the \nparents in this regard; \n(e) the measures being taken by the Government to ensure the data privacy and security of \nthe students’ information collected for APAAR; and \n(f) the details on the benefits of APAAR for students and how it will help them in tracking \ntheir academic journey and achievements? \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF EDUCATION \n(SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n \n \nPart (a) to (f) A Statement is laid on the table of the House. \n \n***** \n  \n\n \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (f) IN RESPECT OF \nLOK SABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. *12 FOR REPLY ON 04.12.2023 \nREGARDING “ONE NATION ONE STUDENT ID” ASKED BY PROF. RITA \nBAHUGUNA JOSHI, DR. SHRIKANT EKNATH SHINDE, HON’BLE MEMBER(S) \nOF PARLIAMENT  \n \n(a) to (f) The Government of India has launched National Educational Policy 2020 with an \naim to provide holistic and multidisciplinary education with multiple entry and exit facility. It \nalso aims to ensure universal access to education at all levels, equitable and inclusive \neducation and lifelong learning ecosystem. \nTo achieve these objectives, a registry framework is required to identify each entity to track \nthe academic and skilling journey of the students/learners throughout his life with many uses \nsuch as transfer of credits, transfer from one institute to other institute etc. It also aims to \nfacilitate and track, the integration of programme with skill component, choice-based courses, \nplanning and improvement in curriculum as per the requirement of stakeholders.   \nAccordingly, Ministry of Education has launched Academic Bank of Credits ( ABC) Scheme \non 29th July 2021 to create unique id for seamless interaction amongst the stakeholders of the \neducation ecosystem. Scheme aims to facilitate flexibility of curriculum framework, multiple \nentry multiple exits, interdisciplinary mobility of the students with appropriate “Credit \ntransfer”, and enables visibility to progress and targeted decision-making at multiple levels. \nDetail process for enrolment for individual students/learners and institutions are available on \nhttps://www.abc.gov.in/. All State Governments have also been communicated with process \nto be followed for enrolment of the students along with the role of the parents in this process.  \n \nData Security and Privacy guidelines prescribed by Ministry of Electronics and Information \nTechnology (MeitY) has been followed to ensure safety and privacy of data.  \n \n \n***** \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S14_U_120": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 120 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 04.12.2023 \n \nREVAMPED BONDED LABOUR REHABILITATION SCHEME IN HARYANA \n \n120.  SHRIMATI SUNITA DUGGAL: \n \nWill the Minister of LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT be pleased to \nstate: \n \n(a)the details of funds released under the revamped Bonded Labour \nRehabilitation Scheme, if so, the details thereof, State/UT -wise \nincluding the State of Haryana; \n(b)the number of beneficiaries under the scheme including Haryana and \nthe amount transferred under Direct Benefit Transfer (DBT); and \n(c)the details and the number of proposals received from State \nGovernments for immediate cash assistance and rehabilitation \nassistance under the scheme, State-wise including Haryana? \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR LABOUR AND EMPLOYMENT \n(SHRI RAMESWAR TELI) \n(a) to (c): The Ministry of Labour & Employment has been \nimplementing a Central Sector Scheme viz. Rehabilitation of Bonded \nLabourer for identification and rehabilitation of bonded labourers. This \nscheme is a demand driven scheme where the rehabilitation assistance \namount is provided by the respective State/Union Territories to the \nrescued bonded labourers which are reimbursed by Central Government \non receipt of proposal from them.  \nUnder the Scheme, rehabilitation assistance to the tune of \nRs. 1.00 lakh, Rs. 2.00 lakh and Rs. 3.00 lakh are provided to each \nrescued bonded labourers by the concerned State/UT Government \nthrough Direct Benefit Transferred (DBT) based on their category and \nlevel of exploitation. The details of number of bonded labourers \nrehabilitated and details of rehabilitation amount released during 2020-\n21 to 2023-24, State-wise, (upto 31.10.2023) is annexed.  \nDuring the last 3 years, no proposal for reimbursement of \nimmediate cash assistance or rehabilitation assistance has been \nreceived from the State Government of Haryana. \n*                                                       ****** \n\n�\n�������� �\n��������� ��������� ��� ��� ������ ��� ����� ���� �� ����� ��� ���� ������\n���������� ��������� ���� ���� ���� ����������� ��� ��������� �������\n������� ���������� ��������� ������� ������� ���������������\n����������������� ��\n�\n����� ��������� ������������������������� �����������������������\n���������������\n�\n�\n�\n��������\n������ ������ ����\n������������ ������ ���\n���������� ������ ���\n����� � ������ ��\n�������\n��������\n������ ���\n�\n�\n�\n��������\n������������� ������ ����\n����������� ������� �����\n������ ��� ����\n���������� ������ ���\n�\n���������\n���������� ������ ���\n�������������� ������� ����\n����������� ������ ����\n��������\n������\n������������\n������������� ������ ���\n����������� ����� ��\n���������� ������ ���\n������\n ",
    "ls|LS17_S14_U_121": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \nDEPARTMENT OF AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 121   \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE 12TH DECEMBER, 2023 \n \nSKILL DEVELOPMENT AMONG FARMERS \n \n* 121.  CH. MEHBOOB ALI KAISER: \nWill the Minister of AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE कृ ͪष एवं ͩकसान कãयाण \nमंğी be pleased to state: \n(a)  the details of schemes being implemented by the Government to promote skill \ndevelopment among farmers in agriculture and allied sectors;  \n(b)  the amount of funds earmarked and spent under the said schemes during each \nof the last three years and the current year; and  \n(c)  the details of initiatives proposed by the Government to increase capacity \nbuilding of farmers? \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER FOR AGRICULTURE AND FARMERS WELFARE \nकृ ͪष एवं ͩकसान कãयाण मंğी           (SHRI ARJUN MUNDA) \n \n(a) to (c):  A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n\nSTATEMENT IN RESPECT OF PARTS (a) TO (c) OF THE LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO 121 FOR 12.12.2023 REGARDING SKILL DEVELOPMENT AMONG \nFARMERS: \n(a) to (c): The Government has initiated and is implementing the following \nschemes aimed to promote skill development and capacity building among farmers in \nthe agriculture and allied sectors: \nA Centrally Sponsored Scheme on ‘Support to State Extension Programmes for \nExtension Reforms’ popularly known as Agriculture Technology Management Agency \n(ATMA) is  implemented across the country. The scheme promotes decentralized \nfarmer-friendly Extension system in the country with an objective to support State \nGovernment’s efforts to revitalize the extension system and making available the latest \nagricultural technologies and good agricultural practices in different thematic areas of \nagriculture and allied areas to farmers. During the last 3 years from 2020-21 to 2022-\n23 and current year 2023-24 (upto November, 2023) 48.07 lakh farmers availed \ntraining benefits under ATMA.   \nThe Government is implementing skill development programmes through Krishi \nVigyan Kendra (KVK) under Indian Council of Agricultural Research (ICAR) in different \nStates of the Country with mandate of technology assessment and demonstration for \nits use and capacity building.  As part of its activities, the KVKs impart training to the \nfarmers, farm women and rural youth on different aspects of agriculture and allied \nsectors for their capacity building. The KVKs trained 73.75 lakh farmers, farm women \nand rural youth during last three years and current year. \nThe Government has launched National Skill Development Mission under the \nMinistry of Skill Development and Entrepreneurship (MSDE) in July 2015, under which \nthe DA&FW has been operationalising skill training courses for rural youth and farmers \nas per the approved Qualification Packs developed by Agriculture Skill Council of India \n(ASCI) in the areas of agriculture and allied sectors through the National Training \nInstitutes (NTIs), State Agriculture Management and Extension Training Institutes \n(SAMETIs), Krishi Vigyan Kendras (KVKs) of Indian Council of Agricultural Research \n(ICAR) and State Agricultural Universities (SAUs).  MSDE, under Pradhan Mantri \nKaushal Vikas Yojana (PMKVY) 9.72 lakh candidates have been trained/oriented \nunder Agriculture and allied sector as on 31.10.2023. \n\nThe Government has launched Skill Training of Rural Youth (STRY) in 2015 \nwith the objective to impart short term skill training (7 days duration inclusive of 1 day \nfor local travel) to rural youths and farmers in agriculture and allied areas for \nupgradation of their knowledge and skills and promote wage/self employment in rural \nareas. The National Institute of Agricultural Extension Management (MANAGE) is \nimplementing STRY across the country through State Agricultural Management & \nExtension Training Institutes (SAMETIs), ATMA and Krishi Vigyan Kendras (KVKs).  \nCentre of Excellence (CoE) for Horticulture is an approved component under \nMission for Integrated Development of Horticulture (MIDH) for different horticulture \ncrops. More than 3.60 lakh farmers have been trained in these centres. There is \nprovision in the Operational Guidelines of Per Drop More Crop (PDMC) for creating \nawareness, organizing training programs, exposure visits etc. to the farmers by the \nstates.   \nAlso under the Sub-Mission on Agricultural Mechanisation (SMAM), a \ncomponent namely ‘Promotion and Strengthening of Agricultural Mechanization \nthrough Training, Testing and Demonstration’ is aimed for skill development \nprogramme in various fields of agriculture mechanisation. During 2020-21 to 2023-24 \n(Upto November, 2023), 52,080 trainees have been trained on various aspects of \nagricultural mechanisation which has helped them in improving their skill levels. The \nGovernment has also recently approved Central Sector Scheme for providing drones \nto the Women Self Help Groups (SHGs) with an outlay of Rs. 1261 Crores. The \nscheme aims to provide trainings and drones to 15000 selected Women SHGs for \nproviding rental services to farmers for agriculture purpose (application of fertilizers \nand pesticides).  \n The Capacity building component of the PM Formalisation of Micro food \nprocessing Enterprises (PMFME) Scheme of Ministry of Food Processing Industries \n(MoFPI) envisages providing 24 Hours/ 3 Days, Food Processing Entrepreneurship \nDevelopment Programme (EDP) Training for, all applicants viz. individuals and Groups \n(Self Help Groups / Farmers Producer Organizations/ Cooperatives). Under the \nPMFME Scheme, a total of 54,767 beneficiaries have been trained till 30th November \n2023.  \n Under National Rural Livelihood Mission (NRLM) of Ministry of Rural \nDevelopment (MoRD), there is provision for training SHGs and Farmers on drone \n\napplications, Natural Farming, Agro Ecological Practices,  Organic Farming,   Millets, \nValue chain Development, Micro irrigation, livestock management, fisheries and \nScientific collection of Non-Timber Forest Produce etc. A total of 1,94,057 Community \nResource Persons were trained on the above activities under the programme.  \n Ministry of Fisheries, Animal Husbandry & Dairying, imparted training to \n12,500 Aquaculture Farmers & Marine Capture Fishermen. \n \n The amount of funds earmarked, spent and farmers  trained under ATMA and \nSkill trainings by DA&FW during 2020-21 to 2023-24 are given at Annexure-I.   \n  \n\nAnnexure-I \nThe amount of funds earmarked, spent and farmers trained under ATMA and Skill \ntrainings by DA&FW during 2020-21 to 2023-24. \n \nYear Funds  \nEarmarked \n(Rs. in \nCrores) \nFunds  Spent \n(Rs. in Crores) \nFarmers trained (Nos.) \n2020-21 845.07 632.67 1398571 \n2021-22 882.74 555.36 1372995 \n2022-23 732.56 478.05 1443795 \n2023-24* 611.23 367.62 635677 \nTOTAL 3071.60 2033.70 4851038 \n \n*Upto November, 2023 \n \n***** ",
    "ls|LS17_S14_U_122": "O.I.H. \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nLOK SABHA \n STARRED QUESTION NO. 122 \n  ANSWERED ON 12/12/2023 \n \nPROGRESS UNDER PMAY-G \n \n*122. SHRI KRUPAL BALAJI TUMANE: \nSHRI RAMSHIROMANI VERMA: \n \nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the progress made under the Pradhan Mantri Awaas Yojana - \nGramin (PMAY-G); \n(b)  whether the Government has any proposal to start the work \nunder its next phase; \n(c)  if so, the details thereof and the time by which the said work is \nlikely to be started in all the villages of Maharashtra and Uttar \nPradesh including Ramtek-Nagpur District in Maharashtra and \nShrawasti Parliamentary Constituency of Uttar Pradesh and \nif not, the reasons therefor; \n(d)  whether the names of the villages of Maharashtra and Uttar \nPradesh including the above said Ramtek-Nagpur District and \nShrawasti Parliamentary Constituency have been finalized \nunder the said yojana, if so, the details thereof and if not, the \nreasons therefor; and \n(e)  the number of houses and the time by which these are likely to \nbe allotted in all the districts including Ramtek-Nagpur District \nin Maharashtra as well as Shrawasti Parliamentary \nConstituency of Uttar Pradesh in the next phase during the \ncoming three years? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT  \n(SHRI GIRIRAJ SINGH) \n \n(a) to  (e):  A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.   \n\nStatement referred to in reply to parts (a) to (e) of Lok Sabha  \nStarred Question No. * 122 to be answered on 12.12.2023 regarding \n“Progress under PMAY-G” \n \n(a)      In order to achieve the target of “Housing for All” in rural \nareas, the Ministry of Rural Development is implementing Pradhan \nMantri Awaas Yojana - Gramin ( PMAY-G) with effect from 1 st April \n2016 to provide assistance to construct 2.95 crore pucca houses \nwith basic amenities. The initial timeline for PMAY -G was March, \n2022, which has now been extended to March 2024. Out of the \noverall target of 2.95 crore hou ses, a target of 2.95 crore houses \nhave been allocated to States/Union Territories (UTs) to date, out of \nwhich, more than 2.94 crore houses have been sanctioned to \nbeneficiaries by various States/UTs and 2.51 crore houses have \nbeen completed as on 07.12.2023. \n(b)      No, Sir. \n(c) to (e)  Do not arise.   \n  \n***** \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S14_U_123": " \n \nGovernment of India \nMinistry of Finance \nDepartment of Revenue \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 123  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON MONDAY , DECEMBER 4, 2023 \nAGRAHAYANA 13, 1945 (SAKA) \n \nTAX HOLIDAY PACKAGE \n \n \n†123. SHRI ASHOK MAHADEORAO NETE: \n  \nWill the Minister of FINANCE be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government proposes to provide tax exemption in central taxes by declaring tax \nholiday package for setting up industries in the Gadchiroli -Chimur tribal Parliamentary \nConstituency of Maharashtra which remains badly affected with Naxalism; \n \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and  \n \n(c) if not, the reasons therefor? \n \n \n \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF FINANCE \n(SHRI PANKAJ CHAUDHARY) \n \n(a) to (c) : There is no such proposal. It is the stated policy of the Government to simplify the \nIncome-tax Act, 1961 by removing exemptions and incentives while at the same time reducing \nthe rates of taxes \n***** ",
    "ls|LS17_S14_U_124": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF TOURISM \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.124 \nANSWERED ON 04.12.2023 \n \nINITIATIVES TO DEVELOP NEW TOURISM SPOTS IN BARDHAMAN \n \n124. SHRI SUNIL KUMAR MONDAL:  \n \nWill the Minister of TOURISM be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the G overnment has any initiative to develop new tourism \nspots in Kalna, Katwa, Raina & Purbosthali -II in Purba Bardhaman, \nWest Bengal;  \n(b) if so, the details thereof along with the present status and if not, the \nreasons therefor;  \n(c) the details of the total  revenue earned from tourism spots in the \ncountry during the last three years and the current year; and \n(d) the funds invested by the Government for developing new tourism \nspots, State/UT-wise and year-wise and if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF TOURISM                                   (SHRI G. KISHAN REDDY) \n \n(a) to (d): The Ministry of Tourism under the schemes of ‘Swadesh \nDarshan’, ‘National Mission on Pilgrimage Rejuvenation and Spiritual \nHeritage Augmentation Drive (PRASHAD)’ and ‘A ssistance to Central \nAgencies for Tourism Infrastructure Development’ provides financial \nassistance to State Governments/Union Territory Administrations/Central \nAgencies for the development of tourism -related infrastructure and \nfacilities at various touris m destinations/spots in the country including \nWest Bengal. \n \n The details of projects sanctioned and amount sanctioned along with \ntheir status under the above -mentioned schemes in the State of West \nBengal is given at Annexure. \n \nData pertaining to revenue ge nerated from tourism is not maintained by \nthe Ministry of Tourism. However, year -wise Foreign Exchange Earnings \n\n(FEEs) from tourism during the last three years including current year \n(upto September 2023) are given below: \n \nYear FEE (Rs. in Crore) \n2020#2 50136 \n2021#2 65070 \n2022#2 139935 \n2023#1 \n(Jan-Sep) \n166660 \n#2: Revised Estimates \n#1: Provisional Estimates \n*********** \n\nANNEXURE \n \nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO ( d) OF LOK SABHA UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 124 ANSWERED ON 0 4.12.2023 REGARDING INITIATIVES \nTO DEVELOP NEW TOURISM SPOTS IN BARDHAMAN  BY SHRI SUNIL \nKUMAR MONDAL  \n \nSwadesh Darshan Scheme         (Rs. in Crore) \nSl. \nNo. \nState Circuit / \nSanction \nYear \nName of the \nProject \nAmount \nSanctioned \nAmount \nReleased \nPhysical \nStatus \n(%) \n1.  West \nBengal \nCoastal \nCircuit \n2015-16 \nDevelopment of \nBeach Circuit: \nUdaipur- Digha- \nShankarpur- \nTajpur- \nMandarmani- \nFraserganj-\nBakkhlai- Henry \nIsland \n67.99 65.07 Complete \n \nPRASHAD Scheme          (Rs. in Crore) \nSl. \nNo. \nState Project Name Sanction \nYear \nApproved \nCost  \nAmount \nReleased  \nPhysical \nProgress \n(%) \n1. West \nBengal \nDevelopment of \nBelur Math \n2016-17 30.03 23.39 92% \n \nAssistance to Central Agencies for Tourism Infrastructure Development \nScheme \n(Rs. in Crore) \nSl. \nNo. \nState Name of \nProjects \nCentral \nAgency \nAmount \nSanctioned \nAmount \nReleased \nStatus \nYear 2017-18    \n1. West \nBengal \nJoint \nDevelopment \nof Rampurhat \nRailway \nStation \nM/o \nRailways \n3.48 1.74 Work \ncompleted. \nHowever, \ncompletion \ncertificate \nis awaited. \n2. West \nBengal \nJoint \nDevelopment \nM/o \nRailways \n3.87 1.93 Ongoing \n\nof \nTarakeshwar \nRailway \nStation \nYear 2019-20    \n3. West \nBengal \nJoint \nDevelopment \nof New \nJalpaiguri \nRailway \nStation \nM/o \nRailways \n4.55 2.27 Recommend\ned by \nMinistry of \nRailways for \nshort \nclosure \nbecause the \nstations are \nselected \nunder Amrit \nBharat \nStation \nScheme  \n****** ",
    "ls|LS17_S14_U_125": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FINANCE \nDEPARTMENT OF FINANCIAL SERVICES \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 125 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON THE DECEMBER 4th, 2023, AGRAHAYANA 13, 1945 (Saka) \n \n‘EDUCATIONAL LOANS BY PUBLIC SECTOR BANKS’ \n125. SHRI BALASHOWRY VALLABHANENI: \nWill the Minister of FINANCE be pleased to state: \n(a) whether it is true that nearly 90 per cent of educational loans are given by Public Sector \nBanks (PSBs);  \n(b) the details of education loan applications received by PSBs, private banks and foreign \nbanks during the last five years, year-wise, bank-wise and State-wise; \n(c) whether the educational loan target for 2022-23 has been reduced by 14 per cent as \ncompared to 2021-22 by the Government; \n(d)  if so, the reasons therefor and the reasons for slow disbursal of educational loans by \nbanks; and \n(e) the reasons that PSBs are not inclined to sanction educational loans without collateral \nand the details of educational loan target set for 2023-24 and progress made so far? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF FINANCE \n(DR. BHAGWAT KARAD) \n \n(a)  As informed by the Indian Bank’s Association (IBA), the share of educational loans \n given by Public Sector Banks (PSBs) under IBA’s Model Education loan scheme for \n pursuing higher education in India and Abroad during FY 2022-23 was \n approximately 83%. \n(b)    Based on the information provided by IBA, the details of education loan applications \n received by PSBs and Private Sector banks during the last five years, year-wise, and \n State-wise is provided at Annex I. \n(c) &(d)  The educational loan disbursement target for FY 2022-23 is Rs.20,450 crore vis-à-\n vis the target Rs. 16,965 crores fixed for FY 2021-22, which represents an increase \n of 20.54 % on a Year-on-Year (YoY) basis. \n (e)  Scheduled Commercial Banks (SCBs) follow IBA’s Model Education Loan Scheme \n for pursuing Higher Education in India and Abroad which, inter-alia, provides \n collateral free loans up to Rs.7.50 lakh. \n \n  Further, as informed by PSBs, they also provide collateral free loan above Rs.7.50 \n  lakhs for premier institutes as per their board approved policies.   \n As against the education loan disbursement target of Rs.29,725 crore for FY 2023-\n 24, Rs.18,083 crore have been disbursed till 31.10.2023 by PSBs. \n \n \n*****\n\nAnnex-I as referred to in Part (b) of the Reply \nNumber of Educational Loan Application Received by Banks during Financial Year \nStates 2018-19 2019-20 2020-21 2021-22 2022-23 \n  PSBs Pvt. Bank Total PSBs Pvt. Bank Total PSBs Pvt. Bank Total PSBs Pvt. Bank Total PSBs Pvt. Bank Total \nAndaman and \nNicobar Islands 49 2 51 72 1 73 47 6 53 108 9 117 308 8 316 \nAndhra Pradesh 18082 1192 19274 18858 1689 20547 14487 1827 16314 22906 2848 25754 43546 3169 46715 \nArunachal Pradesh 70 3 73 62 1 63 35 1 36 59 2 61 116 7 123 \nAssam 2075 103 2178 2735 83 2818 2132 115 2247 2993 169 3162 4723 236 4959 \nBihar 5238 691 5929 5645 989 6634 5508 884 6392 7152 1213 8365 8978 1564 10542 \nChandigarh 739 97 836 849 87 936 559 65 624 800 244 1044 964 645 1609 \nChhattisgarh 2410 162 2572 2821 248 3069 2034 185 2219 2848 245 3093 3930 363 4293 \nDadra & Nagar \nHaveli and Daman \n& Diu 442 11 453 490 7 497 274 4 278 475 25 500 575 21 596 \nDelhi 6248 1339 7587 7610 1535 9145 6736 1436 8172 8591 2998 11589 10292 6304 16596 \nGoa 2142 30 2172 2323 19 2342 1046 12 1058 1281 35 1316 1694 72 1766 \nGujarat 9049 1720 10769 10472 1741 12213 7829 1621 9450 10423 6485 16908 13419 14613 28032 \nHaryana 4117 599 4716 5155 663 5818 4665 766 5431 6771 1218 7989 9293 1840 11133 \nHimachal Pradesh 1289 30 1319 1890 64 1954 1392 43 1435 2120 101 2221 3215 134 3349 \nJammu and Kashmir 724 2011 2735 1067 1723 2790 670 1278 1948 1150 1729 2879 1384 2170 3554 \nJharkhand 6585 425 7010 7095 541 7636 5815 521 6336 7989 757 8746 9986 829 10815 \nKarnataka 21640 2334 23974 29495 2453 31948 23902 2160 26062 36830 3465 40295 4