    "ls|LS17_S14_U_17": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EDUCATION \nDEPARTMENT OF SCHOOL EDUCATION & LITERACY \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO.17 \nANSWERED ON 04.12.2023 \n \nESTABLISHMENT OF SMART CLASSROOMS \nIN KVs AND JNVs IN GUJARAT \n \n17.  SHRI DIPSINH SHANKARSINH RATHOD:  \nSHRI MOHANBHAI KALYANJI KUNDARIYA:  \n \nWill the Minister of EDUCATION be pleased to state:  \n \n(a)  the details of smart classrooms established in Kendriya Vidyalayas (KVs) and Jawahar \nNavodaya Vidyalayas (JNVs) in Gujarat, district-wise;  \n(b)  the number of classrooms of KVs and JNVs equipped with the said smart class system \nin Gujarat, district-wise especially in Rajkot & Sabarkantha districts;  \n(c)  whether the Government is taking steps to introduce the smart class system in all \nclasses of science subjects; and  \n(d)  if so, the timeline by which this project will be implemented? \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF EDUCATION \n(SMT. ANNPURNA DEVI) \n \n(a) & (b) As per information received from Kendriya Vidyalaya Sangathan and \nNavodaya Vidyalaya Samiti, a t present, there are 466 smart classes (e-classrooms) \nestablished in 46 Kendriya Vidyalayas (KVs) and 88 smart classes (e -classrooms) \nestablished in 34 Jawahar Navodaya Vidyalayas  (JNVs) functioning in the State of \nGujarat including Rajkot and Sabarkantha districts. District-wise details of KVs and \nJNVs having e-classrooms are at Annexure-I and Annexure-II, respectively. \n  \n(c) & (d) Setting up of smart class system (including science stream classes) in KVs \nand JNVs is a continuous process which depends upon various factors such as \nopening of new schools, addition of higher classes, availability of funds, availability of \nInternet connectivity etc. and as such no specific time frame can be given in this \nregard.  \n***** \n  \n\nANNEXURE-I \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) & (b) OF THE LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 17 RAISED BY SHRI DIPSINH SHANKARSINH \nRATHOD & SHRI MOHANBHAI KALYANJI KUNDARIYA, HON’BLE MEMBERS OF \nPARLIAMENT ANSWERED ON 04/12/2023 REGARDING ESTABLISHMENT OF \nSMART CLASSROOMS IN KVs AND JNVs IN GUJARAT. \n \nDISTRICT-WISE DETAILS OF SMART CLASSROOMS  \n(E-CLASSROOMS) IN KVs OF GUJARAT \n  \nSl. \nNo. \nName of Districts  Number of E-classrooms in KVs \n1 Ahmedabad 95 \n2 Anand 11 \n3 Banaskantha 8 \n4 Bharuch 18 \n5 Bhavnagar 3 \n6 Dahod  9 \n7 Devbhumi Dwarka 14 \n8 Gandhinagar 45 \n9 Jamnagar 56 \n10 Junagadh 8 \n11 Kachchh  49 \n12 Mehsana 17 \n13 Panchmahal 8 \n14 Porbandar 10 \n15 Rajkot 15 \n16 Sabarkantha 11 \n17 Surat 25 \n18 Surendranagar 11 \n19 Vadodara 53 \nGrand Total 466 \n***** \n  \n\nANNEXURE-II \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) & (b) OF THE LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 17 RAISED BY SHRI DIPSINH SHANKARSINH \nRATHOD & SHRI MOHANBHAI KALYANJI KUNDARIYA, HON’BLE MEMBERS OF \nPARLIAMENT ANSWERED ON 04/12/2023 REGARDING ESTABLISHMENT OF \nSMART CLASSROOMS IN KVs AND JNVs IN GUJARAT.  \n \nDISTRICT-WISE DETAILS OF SMART CLASSROOMS  \n(E-CLASSROOMS) IN JNVs OF GUJARAT \n  \nSl. \nNo. Name of Districts  Number of E-classrooms in JNVs \n1 Ahmedabad 2 \n2 Amreli 2 \n3 Anand 2 \n4 Arvalli 2 \n5 Banaskantha 2 \n6 Bharuch 2 \n7 Bhavnagar 2 \n8 Botad 2 \n9 Chhota Udepur 2 \n10 Dahod  13 \n11 Dang 2 \n12 Devbhumi Dwarka 2 \n13 Gandhinagar 2 \n14 Gir Somnath 2 \n15 Jamnagar 2 \n16 Junagadh 2 \n17 Kachchh  13 \n18 Kheda 2 \n19 Mehsana 2 \n20 Mahisagar 2 \n21 Morbi 2 \n22 Narmada 2 \n23 Navsari 2 \n24 Panchmahal 2 \n25 Patan 2 \n26 Porbandar 2 \n27 Rajkot 2 \n28 Sabarkantha 2 \n29 Surat 2 \n30 Surendranagar 2 \n31 Tapi 2 \n32 Vadodara 2 \n33 Valsad 2 \nGrand Total 88 \n***** \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S14_U_170": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA\nMINISTRY OF CIVIL AVIATION\nLOK SABHA\nSTARRED QUESTION NO. : 170\n(To be answered on the 14th December 2023)\n \nEXPANSION OF PUDUCHERRY AIRPORT\n \n \nWill the Minister of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n(a) the present status of expansion of Puducherry Airport to make larger aircraft operational\ntherefrom;\n(b) the time by which the approval for night landing facility would be extended to Puducherry\nAirport; and\n(c) whether the Ministry is planning to approve few routes under UDAN-RCS to improve the\naircraft operations in Puducherry such as Puducherry-Shirdi, Puducherry-Cochin, Puducherry-\nTirupati and if so, the details of such routes thereof?\n \nANSWER\n \nMinister of CIVIL AVIATION\n \n \n(a) to (c): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House.\n \n*****\n*170. SHRI VE. VAITHILINGAM\n be pleased to state:-\n (Shri Jyotiraditya M. Scindia)\n\nStatement in reply to parts (a) to (c) of the Lok Sabha Starred (*) Question No.170 for answer\non 14.12.2023 regarding 'Expansion of Puducherry Airport':\n \n(a) & (b): The existing airport at Puducherry has a runway length of 1502m which is suitable for\noperation of 72-Seater Q-400/ATR-72 type of aircraft. The extension of its runway upto 3330m\nto make it suitable for operation of A-321 type of aircraft under Instrument Flight Rules (lFR)\nconditions with night landing facility is contingent upon handing over of an additional 395 acre\nof land in Tamil Nadu and 30 acre of land in Puducherry by the respective State\nGovernment/Union Territory Administration. As per National Civil Aviation Policy, 2016, the\nland for development of an airport is to be provided by the respective State Government/ Union\nTerritory Administration free of cost and free from any encumbrances to Airports Authority of\nIndia.\n \n(c): Spicejet Ltd. launched the \"Hyderabad - Puducherry - Hyderabad\" route under the Ude\nDesh ka Aam Nagrik (UDAN) Regional Connectivity Scheme (RCS) on 16.08.2017, and it\ncontinued operations beyond the stipulated 3-year period till date. As the airport's weekly\ndepartures exceeded seven, it no longer qualified as an 'underserved' airport. Consequently, it\nwas excluded from UDAN 5.0, which specifically aimed at enhancing connectivity for unserved\nand underserved airports. Further, Shirdi, Cochin and Tirupati are already designated as\nserved airports and therefore, a pair of served Airports cannot be connected under RCS. In\ncase, any airline bids for connectivity from an unserved or underserved airport to Puducherry\nAirport, it will be considered within the scope of the UDAN RCS.\n*****",
