    "ls|LS17_S14_U_216": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF EDUCATION \nDEPARTMENT OF SCHOOL EDUCATION & LITERACY \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.216 \nANSWERED ON 18.12.2023 \n \nEducation of Children having Mental/Neuro Disorder under NEP  \n \n†*216. SHRI GUMAN SINGH DAMOR:  \n \nWill the Minister of EDUCATION be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the provision in the New Education Policy for special children suffering from mental/neuro \ndisorders; \n(b) whether special training is being imparted to teachers appointed to teach such children;  \n(c) if so, the details thereof and if not, whether the Government will consider the same;  \n(d) whether the Government proposes to provide employment oriented education to such \nchildren;  \n(e) if so, the details thereof; and  \n(f) if not, whether the Government will consider the same? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF EDUCATION \n(SHRI DHARMENDRA PRADHAN) \n \n \n(a) to (f): A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (A) TO (F) OF THE LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 216 FOR REPLY ON 18.12.2023 ASKED BY SHRI GUMAN \nSINGH DAMOR , HON’BLE MEMBER OF PARLIAMENT REGARDING \n‘EDUCATION OF CHILDREN HAVING MENTAL/NEURO DISORDER UNDER NEP’. \n \n(a) to (c) The National Education Policy (NEP) 2020 is in complete consonance with the \nprovisions of the Rights of Persons wit h Disabilities  (RPwD) Act, 2016 and endorses all its \nrecommendations with regard to school education.  \n Education is in the concurrent list of the Constitution and majority of the schools are \nunder the domain of respective State and UT Governments. State a nd UT Governments are the \nappropriate Governments under the Right of Children to Free and Compulsory Education (RTE) \nAct, 2009.  \n The Centrally Sponsored Scheme of Samagra  Shiksha launched in 2018 -19, has \ndedicated Inclusive Education component for the edu cation of Children with Special Needs (IE \nfor CwSN)  covering all CwSN  with one or more disabilities as mentioned in the schedule of \ndisabilities of the RPwD Act, 2016 including children with neuro -disorders like cerebral palsy, \nautism spectrum disorder and disability caused due to chronic neurological conditions. It aims to \nlook at education of CwSN in a continuum from Pre -Primary to Class XII  studying in \nGovernment, Government-aided and local body schools.  \n The good education, particularly for children wi th neuro-disorders like ASD and ADHD \nstarts with the screening at the school, which in turn may lead to identification and certification \nof the disability making them eligible for the provisions under inclusive education component of \nSamagra Shiksha to sup port their learning in the nearby inclusive school.  The screening of \nstudents with special needs including children with ASD and SLD is currently being done \nthrough the PRASHAST App. \nCapacity building of general teachers and special educators on meeting le arning needs to \nprovide quality education to children with special needs and improve their learning outcomes, \nare also covered. There is a dedicated National Initiative for School Heads' and Teachers' \nHolistic Advancement (NISHTHA) Module which aims to bui ld competencies among all the \nteachers and school principals at the elementary stage. A five -day Capacity Building Programme \nfor general teachers in Inclusive Education has been included in NISHTHA - Equitable and \nInclusive Education for 2023-24. \n  \n(d) to (f) With a view to provide quality vocational training with high employability focusing \nonly on P erson with Disabilities , the National Action Plan for Skill Development of PwDs \n(NAP-SDP), a dedicated skill development programme for PwDs was launched by the  \nDepartment of Empowerment of Persons with Disabilities (DEPwD) in March 2015. The key \nobjectives of the Scheme are:  \na. To enhance skills of Persons with Disabilities; provisioning of quality vocational Skill \nTraining to Divy